      "id": 1,
      "text": "Remington sits on the Rappahannock River, offering scenic river access and preserved Civil War history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.remington-va.gov/things-to-experience",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was once called Rappahannock Station when the Orange and Alexandria Railroad ran through it, later renamed Remington.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.remingtonva.com/history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Remington was the site of the First and Second Battles of Rappahannock Station during the Civil War.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Remington%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Historic buildings in Remington showcase Victorian styles with bay windows, turrets, and painted‑lady color schemes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.remington-va.gov/things-to-experience",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Rappahannock Canal once made Remington a commercial port, but the canal failed and was abandoned.",
